^^ = and ordering operators.  Without `when` (Part 3) a condition can only be
^^ reported; Phase 1 prints an empty line for it, so the native code must too.
^^ Each comparison is still evaluated, so the runtime single-base check runs.
gene nucleus()
    "ACGT" -> dna g
    report g = "ACGT"
    report head(g) < 'C'
    report g@3 >= 'G'
    "G" -> dna b
    report b <= g@2           ^^ b holds one base: passes the runtime check
    report g                  ^^ ACGT
stop
